{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators","id":181691,"title":"Can't understand the Integrators","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T23:21:02-07:00","id":181691,"title":"Can't understand the Integrators","content":"Ok, you want to go back to the God machine. But you want to retain free will. There's next to no possibility that will happen. Why should I want someone who wants to betray us in our ring?<br /> I mean...Integrators seem to me more of a &quot;counter-splat&quot;, like Banishers, Bale hounds, Seers of the Throne and Loyalists...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T23:40:09-07:00","id":181717,"title":"","content":"I point to Saboteurs.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's next to no possibility that will happen,&quot; you say.<br /> <br /> Does this come before or after the Integrators' stereotypical opposite numbers having ambitions of <i>killing God</i>?<br /> <br /> &quot;Why should I want someone who wants to betray us in our ring?&quot; you ask.<br /> <br /> Is this a question being asked in good faith, or would &quot;Why should I want someone in our ring who wants to draw attention to us and destroy the group's cohesion?&quot; be met with an indignant reaction?<br /> <br /> Because that's a proportionately &quot;accurate&quot; description of the Thugs and it has about as much to do with actual Saboteurs as &quot;someone who wants to betray us&quot; does with actual Integrators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-27-2014, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:17:41-07:00","id":181802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=181717#post181717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I point to Saboteurs.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's next to no possibility that will happen,&quot; you say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, a Saboteur can still be an Integrator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this come before or after the Integrators' stereotypical opposite numbers having ambitions of <i>killing God</i>? </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't follow you. Could you please rephrase?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Why should I want someone who wants to betray us in our ring?&quot; you ask.<br /> <br /> Is this a question being asked in good faith, or would &quot;Why should I want someone in our ring who wants to draw attention to us and destroy the group's cohesion?&quot; be met with an indignant reaction?<br /> <br /> Because that's a proportionately &quot;accurate&quot; description of the Thugs and it has about as much to do with actual Saboteurs as &quot;someone who wants to betray us&quot; does with actual Integrators. </div> </div> </div>Well, I see it like this. As an Integrator, you actually like the God Machine. If it weren't for free will, you'd probably be willing to be recycled and return to be an angel, and start doing shit like before you Fell. Why would I trust someone who could easily decide to aid the God Machine?<br /> What exactly tells you that you will be able to become a free-willed angel? What kind of success do you think you'll be able to achieve in pursuing this mission against a clearly overwhelming force? Is it realistic for your plan to succed, book-wise?<br /> I mean, Saboteurs are more clearly to be trusted, because they actively want to disrupt the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-27-2014, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T06:19:51-07:00","id":181852,"title":"","content":"Don't forget denial. &quot;Life was so much better back then, I didn't have doubt, didn't have to hide on my own...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T06:40:18-07:00","id":181875,"title":"","content":"Have you read their Flowers of Hell expanded description? It went quite a long way to making Integrators more feasible in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:05:10-07:00","id":181906,"title":"","content":"I do not possess Flowers of Hell at the moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:23:16-07:00","id":181926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=181906#post181906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not possess Flowers of Hell at the moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My deepest sympathies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:28:11-07:00","id":181983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators#post181691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should I want someone who wants to betray us in our ring?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you know they want to betray you? When two demons meet there is no way to know the other's Agenda unless they tell you, and of course even then they may be lying. The book even mentions possibly playing with the agendas secret from the other players rather than just the characters.<br /> <br /> I think that is very in-theme for an espionage horror game. Any of your 'friends' could be double agents or at least want to be double agents and you can't really know they aren't. Hell, when you first meet them, you wouldn't even know they were a demon let alone what their motives might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T14:34:14-07:00","id":182235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=181802#post181802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point, a Saboteur can still be an Integrator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not my point. \u200bThe Soldiers and the Idealists are the two Agendas with the most extremists in their ranks. That necessarily means that they're going to be easy to paint as analogs to other splats' antagonist groups. The Thugs are tantamount to bridge-burners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, I don't follow you. Could you please rephrase? </div> </div> </div>There is an entire sidebar on page 47 of the Demon corebook that makes scoffing at any demon's plans extra silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I see it like this. As an Integrator, you actually like the God Machine. </div> </div> </div>As an Integrator, you see the systems of the God-Machine as useful to your goals. What that means for your feelings on <i>the God-Machine as an entity</i> is highly variable.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, let's actually look at the lexicon for a moment, because the operative conflict between the Turncoats and the Thugs is decidedly broader than &quot;these guys hate the Machine, these guys want to rejoin the Machine, let's you and him fight&quot;:<br /> <br /> Integrators: an Agenda; demons who wish to reunite with the God-Machine, <b>subvert it, change it for the better,</b> or take their old place as angels.<br /> Saboteurs: an Agenda; demons who wish to disrupt the God-Machine\u2019s plans by <b>preventing it from creating Infrastructure and occult matrices.</b><br /> <br /> If your plans include &quot;trick the giant miracle-engine into making magic that serves my purposes,&quot; you are by necessity going to come into conflict with someone whose plans include &quot;destroy the system that makes impossibilities happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it weren't for free will, you'd probably be willing to be recycled and return to be an angel, and start doing shit like before you Fell. Why would I trust someone who could easily decide to aid the God Machine? </div> </div> </div>Because literally the only difference between the Turncoats and the rest of the Agendas is that they are more likely to have a reason for stabbing you in the back that you can immediately discern which is not &quot;I don't have to outrun the bear.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly tells you that you will be able to become a free-willed angel? </div> </div> </div>Exiles demonstrably exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kind of success do you think you'll be able to achieve in pursuing this mission against a clearly overwhelming force? Is it realistic for your plan to succed, book-wise?<br /> I mean, Saboteurs are more clearly to be trusted, because they actively want to disrupt the God Machine. </div> </div> </div>Saboteurs include among their number demons who want to <i>end existence.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:34:46-07:00","id":182359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators#post181691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, you want to go back to the God machine. But you want to retain free will. There's next to no possibility that will happen. Why should I want someone who wants to betray us in our ring?<br /> I mean...Integrators seem to me more of a &quot;counter-splat&quot;, like Banishers, Bale hounds, Seers of the Throne and Loyalists...</div> </div> </div> </div> Next to no possibility? That's your problem right there. You're assuming the chances are small. You're also assuming that they want to retain free will, and not some other goal, such as reprogramming the local God Machine processes, or they believe that demons still serve the God Machine, but in a different capacity. In Demon, there's a very strong chance that Integrators can pull it off. You have the ability to - the only problem is that your opponents have bigger guns.<br /> <br /> I don't see the Integrators as the counter-splat, but more like the &quot;sin-eating&quot; splat: Lancea Sanctum, Guardians of the Veil, or the Winter Court. They're involved in doing suspicious things for the right reasons.<br /> <br /> Integrators are the ones most likely to think and act like Fallen Angels, instead of Demons. <br /> <br /> And I agree with Satchel - you are painting the Saboteurs with a rose-colored brush. They're driven by HATE. They want to bring down the God-Machine at any cost. Lets not forget that the G-M saved humanity from the Y2K bug and astroids with the power to destroy all life on earth. Lets not forget that, should God-Machine die, there's a good chance that there's something worse out there that's waiting to fill the void. Lets not forget that tearing down Infrastructure tends to have backlashes like, oh, earthquakes and major fires starting up.<br /> <br /> How could you trust someone that's so deep in hate that they find all this collateral damage and lives lost acceptable?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:40:19-07:00","id":182364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=181802#post181802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I see it like this. As an Integrator, you actually like the God Machine. If it weren't for free will, you'd probably be willing to be recycled and return to be an angel, and start doing shit like before you Fell. Why would I trust someone who could easily decide to aid the God Machine?</div> </div> </div> </div> Integrators include members who want to hook themselves up to the God Machine because they believe that they can reprogram it to be the Kind and Loving God that people believe to exist. Wouldn't that be a hell of a coup to pull off? Especially when they know its more than possible?<br /> <br /> That has nothing to do with &quot;liking&quot; the God Machine so much as realizing that there's options for doing things on your own terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would also like to point out that the best &quot;Angel Breakers&quot; aren't the Tempters, but rather an Integrator / Saboteur mix. +3 bonus for thinking like an angel, +3 for causing the G-M's system to break down by earning a Fall. Despite reputations as angel breakers, Tempters lack any bonuses that'd help them. So, food for thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-27-2014, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:43:48-07:00","id":182367,"title":"","content":"Think about it this way: the God-Machine has tendrils and agents in damn near every facet of the universe. Imagine what you could do with all that, if inly you re-Integrated and had it at your fingertips! Many Integrators don't want to be recycled (tantamount to suicide) or to return to mundane Angel existence; they wish to retain their free will and continue to exist, just as the whole beings they once were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:40:22-07:00","id":183155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=182364#post182364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to point out that the best &quot;Angel Breakers&quot; aren't the Tempters, but rather an Integrator / Saboteur mix. +3 bonus for thinking like an angel, +3 for causing the G-M's system to break down by earning a Fall. Despite reputations as angel breakers, Tempters lack any bonuses that'd help them. So, food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of derail: the reason the Tempters have a reputation for aiming to precipitate Falls is that they're the Agenda most concerned with sensation, feeling, and other worldly matters.<br /> <br /> Y'know, the things most every demon Fell for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:13:08-07:00","id":183173,"title":"","content":"Integrators might have been an antagonist group had the God-Machine learned to differentiate between demonic Agendas. Unfortunately, that's just not possible.<br /> <br /> Enemy of my enemy leads to sharing the same bed, even if the shared enemy is 'home' for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T23:54:05-07:00","id":189221,"title":"","content":"It's funny but this exact topic was discussed by Matt McFarland and Rose Baily in the Darker Days Radio Podcast #53. If you're still interested in trying to understand the Integrator mindset then I'd recommend giving it a listen. I personally like the chit-chat parts of the podcast but if you'd like to just skip to your quandary then the time mark is 50:23.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T21:44:08-07:00","id":191973,"title":"","content":"Especially after reading the Flowers section of Integrators I have started to think that the only real reason for them to survive amongst the rest of the Demon Agendas is by hiding their true allegiance. While each Demon is basically looking out for number 1 and is thus likely to betray others if need be only the Integrators seem to be based on the fact that they not only will but must betray the rest of their kind, leaving me to wonder why the rest of the Agendas do not actively hunt down known Integrators. The important thing here being that the members of the other Agendas <u><i><b>may</b></i></u> betray you for their own benefit but the Integrators <u><i><b>will</b></i></u> betray you. It really matters little how they explain their betrayal to themselves, trying to redeem the G-M etc. as it makes zero difference to those ring members being dismantled for spare parts by the G-M.<br /> <br /> So basically I agree with those who think that the only real way for an Integrator to be a part of a ring consisting of non-integrator members is by concealing his Agenda, which of course comes naturally to Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T22:10:44-07:00","id":192003,"title":"","content":"So long as an Integrator said from the get-go &quot;I want to redeem the God-Machine,&quot; I can see some rings accepting them; it certainly beats a &quot;surprise, I want to work for our old boss!&quot; moment. I can see some Inquisitors seeing the value in keeping an Integrator around as an Angel specialist, and they have good reason to trade info about Infrastructure with each other. They're not all &quot;the God-Machine is perfect and I cannot wait to murder all of you guys!&quot; types, y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T03:24:22-07:00","id":192220,"title":"","content":"The Flowers parts of the Integrators are a bit.... Mixed up. The first part, that talks about them in play, treats them as if they are already traitors and time bombs. The second part, that talks about their versions of achieving Hell, actually are at odds with the Integrators In Play part. IIP assumes that the Integrator wants to be back in the God Machine's good graces. The entire section is devoted to that &quot;Reconciler&quot; stance. The Philosophy section, however, paints a different view - that the GM is broken, not divine, or killable from the inside. <br /> <br /> The In Play section also assumes that you will be earning Angel Empathy beats by screwing over your ring. &quot;Beat: Take a Beat when the character puts the ring at risk or makes the ring vocally or actively suspicious of his motives&quot;. Like I said before, Angel Empathy makes Integrators the best angel-breakers. You actively gain beats by putting the Ring at risk when angel jacking, getting the angels to Fall, and resolving Angel Empathy gets big clues on what would induce a Fall (sorry Satchel, but physical temptations are not the number 1 reason; it's just one of many). <br /> <br /> The problem comes from the whole &quot;make ring suspicious of you&quot; bits. You can do that just by acting like a lone wolf - don't talk about why you do stuff. But that gets you kicked out. It's ironic that the the ones most dependent on rings for beats are the ones most likely to be kicked out for it. Unlike Interrogators, you can't really get a ring of all Integrators going, since they tend to support each other rather than be suspicious. <br /> <br /> In either case, earning suspicion is why Integrators aren't upfront about why they do stuff. They may want to become an exile, or fix the GM, or something equitable. But the Angel Empathy condition pretty much requires them to be secretive, more so than other Demons. So, yeah. Integrators hide who they are. Not because they necessarily will screw over the ring, but because it's part of their nature. <br /> <br /> I also question the whole &quot;good graces&quot; thing. This implies that the God Machine can effectively be bribed. It's been known to give mortals rewards in exchange for service. Can it knowingly make an unchained demon into an exile? Or give access to a method of integration that would altar the God Machine unknown Mission itself? I think a major part of the problem with understanding the Turncoats is &quot;how do they Integrate without being recycled?&quot; And no small bit of question over how to fix or upgrade the GM's methods. Achieving Hell for all agendas needs to be addressed, I think. Otherwise, Saboteurs are the only ones that make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T13:54:00-07:00","id":192729,"title":"","content":"<b>MCN</b>,<br /> <br /> You make some interesting point about hiccups with the Angel Empathy mechanic and rewarded mortal mechanic. However, I personally believe that those issues are more down to the roleplayers and the storyteller to resolve than issues with the Integrator Agenda as a whole. In my research I've concluded that the one truth of the God Machine is that it tries to generate Output as efficiently as possible, and as such all decisions it makes is based around the question: &quot;How can this be accomplish with the least effort.&quot; Since the God Machine is also inscrutable about what Output it's trying to make that leave the hows and whys directly in the storytellers hands. As for Angelic Empathy I believe it was designed that way to allow players to try and find their own way back to Heaven without forcing them to one behavior or another. If they betray the party or simply appear to be working against the Ring then it should be to further that individual Demon's personal Descent. If an Integrator's plans to rejoin the God Machine revolves around, &quot;Betraying my Ringmates to the God Machine&quot; then they've just made antagonistic characters and should suffer the full consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> It should be important to also note the following: <br /> <br /> <b>All Demons Lie</b><br /> <br /> I think we can all agree that of all creatures in heaven and earth the Unchained are the least likely to trust another Demon. I personally think it wouldn't be to far fetched to say that a Ring of Demons on a fundamental level considers their Ringmates as just stepping stone on their own path to Hell. This would makes sense seeing as all Demons were once Angels who would use any means to complete their mission, including lying and using unwitting pawn for no other reason than efficiency. I feel the reason Demons have any personal ties to their Fallen piers at all is because of the human element that's integrated into them when they Fall. A Demon could plot for centuries to accomplish an operation against the God Machine and it's Angels, but they must experience those centuries as a human, with human need and human fears. The human element is what differentiates the scumbags from the would be heroes, and in the World of Darkness there's a very thin line between the two for even regular humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T16:45:14-07:00","id":192889,"title":"","content":"I've always thought of integrators as Michael Westin during the earlier seasons of Burn Notice. His team trusts him because he's him and they have history - plus it's clear there's a lot standing between him and rejoining the CIA/Machine. Though this raises the interesting question of what informant-period Sam would be - a tempter who trades secrets to angels for protection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T17:37:38-07:00","id":192903,"title":"","content":"Something I don't often see mentioned is the idea that many Integrators might be of the &quot;return to the God-Machine after I achieve X&quot; variety. Take the demon in City Planning (from the Core fiction bits). He clearly feels like he made a mistake in his act of rebellion, but rather than turning himself over to the hunters he has chosen to take personal responsibility for saving the city under his protection from that mistake.<br /> <br /> An Integrator's goal could be quite long term (as it is in the Untimely fiction bit from the Core) or even open-ended (such as a demon who has designated herself a righter of wrongs in a region). Even if a demon has a set, achievable goal nothing says he won't move the goal posts, putting off the day of judgment time and again - setting just one more little goal before he takes a bow and leaves the stage. Or a demon might put off pursuing her stated goal at all like the person who &quot;has a novel in her&quot; that she never gets around to writing.<br /> <br /> In essence, that kind of Integrator has no reason to betray other demons. He may want to go back to the God-Machine, sure, but not today. He has so much left to do before he goes, and he has just as much of an interest in staying ahead of the hunter angels pursuing him as the most stalwart Saboteur does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:36:47-07:00","id":193431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=192729#post192729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>MCN</b>You make some interesting point about hiccups with the Angel Empathy mechanic and rewarded mortal mechanic. However, I personally believe that those issues are more down to the roleplayers and the storyteller to resolve than issues with the Integrator Agenda as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div> .... What does that have to do with Integrators being portrayed as overwhelmingly all backstabers who achieve their ascension by selling out their fellow demons? Despite there being overwhelming other ways to play it other than an angelic Judas? <br /> <br /> There's a discrepancy between the Integrators In Play write up, and how I've seen Integrator characters portrayed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>All Demons Lie</b> </div> </div> </div> All demons lie. However, only Integrators are portrayed as consistently selling their fellows out to the enemy. The Flowers write up seems to portray them more as the equivalent to Loyalists or Privateers from Changeling, rather than something akin to the Winter Court. Delusional Black hats. Other agendas may backstab you, steal your stuff to further their own goals, but at least they usually won't sell you out to the Enemy AS their goal. Integrators will. <br /> <br /> <br /> The question I was trying to address is this : Why are Integrators consistently portrayed this way in the books, when there are so many other viable options? Especially in a role playing game that relies to an extent that you can trust your fellows at the table; otherwise, there's no game going on. <br /> <br /> <br /> The only reason that I can see for Integrators selling out their fellow Unchained to angels is that the celestial bureaucracy can be bribed or blackmailed into getting what the Integrator wants. If you can become an Exile, or &quot;fix&quot; the God Machine, or whatever, by selling out your fellow Unchained. <br /> <br /> <br /> There's either a significant piece of the puzzle we're missing here, or the portrayal is one dimensional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:41:07-07:00","id":193432,"title":"","content":"Don't know if this has already been suggested, but what if Integrators weren't so much interested in rejoining the God-Machine as they were seeking service with a divine patron? Whether Yahweh, Vishnu, or some other deity, maybe even the one that the Qashmallim serve, seeing it as the true source of order and righteousness as opposed to the Demiurge of the machine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:48:23-07:00","id":193436,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, this thread has caused me to revise a character concept I've been toying with. Instead of a Paranoid/Tempter, I now feel that Integrator/Tempter would be a better fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T17:38:17-07:00","id":194142,"title":"","content":"<b>MCN</b>, <br /> <br /> I feel that our major disagreement come from the fact that I actually haven't read Flowers of Hell yet. All of the information I've use for my topics has exclusively come from the Demon: the Descent core rulebook. From what I've read though all of the Agenda's have been portrayed pretty evenhandedly, each one given two monikers to represent one idealistic quality and one...not so idealistic quality. I honestly don't see any part of the book where the Integrator's have been portrayed as negatively as you say. I feel that the angelic judases your talking about are the Compromised Agencies. They are the Privateer/Loyalist equivalent for Demon, but a Compromised Agency isn't just full of antagonistic Integrators though. The scary thing about them is that any Agency could become Compromised, and it plays on the same Axiom from Changeling that states: &quot;Anything is better than going back to Faerie.&quot;<br /> However, I would be lying if I didn't say I had a slight bias in favor of the Integrators, as expressed by my avatar, and like I said I haven't gotten my hands onto Flowers yet so I could be wrong and they are all supposed to be depicted as double agents. Although it does seem to go against the shades of grey mentality that perpetuates the nWoD setting and it's protagonists. I just feel that there are as many Idealists as there are Turncoats in Demon: the Descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T23:41:06-07:00","id":194387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=193432#post193432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know if this has already been suggested, but what if Integrators weren't so much interested in rejoining the God-Machine as they were seeking service with a divine patron? Whether Yahweh, Vishnu, or some other deity, maybe even the one that the Qashmallim serve, seeing it as the true source of order and righteousness as opposed to the Demiurge of the machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's brought up as an Integrator school of thought in Flowers of Hell - that is, that there's a true divinity beyond the God-Machine (or true divinities, for those who align to a more animist perspective like Shinto).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T14:06:51-07:00","id":198218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181691-can-t-understand-the-integrators?p=192220#post192220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(sorry Satchel, but physical temptations are not the number 1 reason; it's just one of many).</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;physical temptations.&quot;<br /> <br /> I said &quot;sensation, feeling, and other worldly matters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Recall that angels are highlighted as occupying a somewhat paradoxical expected space wherein they have to be God's point of contact with the world while also remaining disconnected from it.<br /> <br /> Recall that over half of the sample catalysts concern emotional reactions that the nascent demon's scrubbing didn't catch.<br /> <br /> Recall that the Tempters are the primary advocates for demons (or at least themselves) being able to live life according to one's own preferences.<br /> <br /> Angels are preoccupied with their Purpose. Saboteurs take that leftover urge and throw themselves into tossing their collective shoes into the workings of the Machine. Integrators pick up the banner of reclaiming a Purpose with or from the Machine. Inquisitors aim to escape the grasp of the Machine.<br /> <br /> Tempters do as the Inquisitors do, but aim to make a life for themselves along the way.<br /> <br /> A Tempter can tell you exactly why he likes the simple life of a dock worker, and he almost certainly knows a guy who can get a wavering angel the things it always wanted out of existence, whether that's a loving family, the ability to set its own hours, or a superior who isn't cryptic to the point of disaster.<br /> <br /> An Integrator can tell you that the angel will prioritize searching the sedan by the end of the lot over intercepting the cat you're going to use to send a call for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}